  "notes": "Whole physical Bujagali dam and integral open-air powerhouse/intake: complete original49control main dam boundary, full connected11control/~899m crest route, five-unit169x39m named plant envelope, main gated spillway/weir and emergency siphon spillway. Primary construction designers/engineer/contractor describe30m clay-core rockfill and concrete gravity sections, three rockfill sections, two radial/one flap main gates, emergency spillway, five Kaplan units, integral intake and explicitly open-air powerhouse inside dam body. No generic roofed industrial shed or bare embankment proxy. Exact native outer body/route and narrow plant envelope retained; the latter is taggedpower=plant, not a surveyed architectural footprint, so its precise role/internal divisions and all floor/vertical/slope/bay/finish/grade details are explicitly estimated. Whole intrinsic dam/intake/powerhouse/spillways included. Detached substation, transmission lines, wider industrial site/buildings, river/reservoir, former falls and interiors excluded as separate objects. No imagery used or photographic fidelity claimed."
